<item>
  <title>Honne and Tatemae</title>
  <link>https://guitars.volumen.ca/posts/2026-06-21/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 




<p>Tempo: 85 bpm<br>
Score: <a href="honne_and_tatemae.pdf">Download</a><br>
MuseScore: <a href="honne_and_tatemae.mscz">Download</a></p>
<section id="video" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="video">Video</h2>
<p>Just the Amp and Trem Pedal:</p>
<p>60 bpm</p>
<div class="quarto-video ratio ratio-16x9"><iframe data-external="1" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/TccAJh9Ursw" title="" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div>
<div class="quarto-video ratio ratio-16x9"><iframe data-external="1" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/Ko--WiylY4U" title="" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div>
<div class="quarto-video ratio ratio-16x9"><iframe data-external="1" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/IyfD4Sphpks" title="" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div>
<div class="quarto-video ratio ratio-16x9"><iframe data-external="1" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/UvvrcpthfsU" title="" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div>
<div class="quarto-video ratio ratio-16x9"><iframe data-external="1" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/E1TWdCgtcvE" title="" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div>
</section>
<section id="fender-telecaster" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="fender-telecaster">Fender Telecaster</h2>
<p>Pickup Position: Neck</p>
</section>
<section id="zoom-g3xn" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="zoom-g3xn">Zoom G3Xn</h2>
<p>150 Trem Etc</p>
</section>
<section id="joyo-tremolo" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="joyo-tremolo">Joyo Tremolo</h2>
<p>Intensity: 50%<br>
Rate: 50%</p>
</section>
<section id="fender-blues-jr.-iii" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="fender-blues-jr.-iii">Fender Blues Jr.&nbsp;III</h2>
<p>Volume: 3.5<br>
Fat: OFF<br>
Treble: 4.5<br>
Bass: 7.0<br>
Middle: 11.0<br>
Master: 3.5<br>
Reverb: 2.0</p>
</section>
<section id="blue-yeti" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="blue-yeti">Blue Yeti</h2>
<p>Gain: 9 o’clock<br>
Mode: Cardioid mode, 12” from speaker, slightly off-axis</p>
</section>
<section id="dolby-on" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="dolby-on">Dolby ON</h2>
<p>OFF</p>
</section>
<section id="zoom-g3xn-princeton-warm-patch-checklist" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="zoom-g3xn-princeton-warm-patch-checklist">Zoom G3Xn “Princeton Warm” Patch Checklist</h2>
<p>Guitar: MIJ Tele, neck pickup, volume/tone slightly rolled back Amp: Fender Blues Jr III (miked — no Zoom amp/cab sim used) Goal: warm, articulate Princeton Reverb-style clean tone with shimmer trem and spring reverb</p>
</section>
<section id="signal-chain" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="signal-chain">Signal Chain</h2>
<p>Guitar → RackComp → RC Boost → Tremolo → FD Spring → Zoom output → Blues Jr input → mic</p>
</section>
<section id="block-1-rackcomp-dynamics" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="block-1-rackcomp-dynamics">Block 1 — RackComp (DYNAMICS)</h2>
<ul class="task-list">
<li><label><input type="checkbox">THRSH: 25–30</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Ratio: 3–4:1</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">ATTCK: 5–6 (mid-slow, lets pick transient through before compressing)</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">VOL: 100 (unity — no boost here)</label></li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="block-2-rc-boost-drive" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="block-2-rc-boost-drive">Block 2 — RC Boost (DRIVE)</h2>
<ul class="task-list">
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Gain: 15–20 (just enough to nudge the amp, not add drive character)</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Bass: 50</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Treble: 55–60</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">VOL: 105–110 (small push, +2–4 dB feel)</label></li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="block-3-tremolo-modulation" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="block-3-tremolo-modulation">Block 3 — Tremolo (MODULATION)</h2>
<ul class="task-list">
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Wave: <strong>TUBE</strong></label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Depth: 35–40</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Rate: 30–35</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">VOL: 100</label></li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="block-4-fd-spring-reverb" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="block-4-fd-spring-reverb">Block 4 — FD Spring (REVERB)</h2>
<ul class="task-list">
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Color: try 0 first, switch to 1 if thin</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Lo: 55–60</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Hi: 45–50</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Mix: 30–35</label></li>
</ul>
<p>Alternative if FD Spring sounds too metallic: swap in plain <strong>Spring</strong> - PreD: 10–15 - Decay: 12–15 - Mix: 30–35</p>
</section>
<section id="amp-settings-blues-jr-iii" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="amp-settings-blues-jr-iii">Amp Settings — Blues Jr III</h2>
<ul class="task-list">
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Volume: 4–5</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Fat: OFF</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Treble: 5.5–6</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Bass: 4.5–5</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Middle: 5–6</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Master: 4–4.5</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Reverb: OFF or very low (FD Spring on the Zoom is handling reverb — avoid stacking two reverbs)</label></li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="mic-setup-blue-yeti-on-stock-desktop-stand-floor-placement" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="mic-setup-blue-yeti-on-stock-desktop-stand-floor-placement">Mic Setup — Blue Yeti (on stock desktop stand, floor placement)</h2>
<ul class="task-list">
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Mode: Cardioid</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Orientation: <strong>logo side of mesh grille facing the amp</strong> (this is the capsule’s listening face — confirmed correct)</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Distance: 4–5 inches from grille</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Position: base shifted slightly to the <strong>right</strong> of the amp’s centerline (creates true off-axis angle, since the stock stand doesn’t swivel sideways)</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Tilt: forward, toward the amp — this aims the capsule up to cone height (compensating for the stand sitting lower than the speaker on the floor)</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Gain: set using the <em>loudest</em> tremolo peak, target -12 to -6 dB, no clipping</label></li>
</ul>
<p>Notes: - Forward tilt = vertical aim adjustment (reaches cone height), not the off-axis angle - Sideways base offset = true off-axis angle (softens pick attack/harshness) - Both adjustments are used together in this floor setup since the stand can’t swivel independently</p>
</section>
<section id="test-pass" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="test-pass">Test Pass</h2>
<ul class="task-list">
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Record 15–20 seconds of comping/chords</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">RC Boost check: should be inaudible as a “pedal” — felt as amp push, not as added grit. If gritty, lower Gain further.</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Reverb check: confirm only FD Spring is audible, not doubled with Blues Jr reverb</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Tremolo check: TUBE wave should feel smoother/rounder than a standard triangle wave trem</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Compression check: RackComp should be felt as sustain/evenness, not obvious pumping</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Overall: does the amp feel like it’s “working” a little (natural compression) rather than stiff/clean?</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">If still too clean/stiff: raise Master first, before touching EQ</label></li>
</ul>


</section>

<a onclick="window.scrollTo(0, 0); return false;" id="quarto-back-to-top"><i class="bi bi-arrow-up"></i> Back to top</a> ]]></description>
